+# Master goal slice — voxel-world water color removal + typed-geometry regression guard (2026-09-20)
+
+## Task
+Bounded Implementation/test slice for the master goal (hourly factory, issue #80): cut the dead per-vertex `color` attribute from voxel-world water meshes and lock the merged voxel perf family's typed-attribute contract with a focused regression test.
+
+## Why
+- Architect lane (issue #80, 2026-09-17) "voxel vertex-color quantization (Uint8)" is already merged on master (makeGeometry now uploads `color` as normalized Uint8, position Int16, normal Int8, uv Uint16, shared Uint16 index).
+- Remaining safe gap found during inspection: the `water` buffer still gathers a `color` attribute even though `waterMaterial` is `vertexColors:false` and its custom shader repaints color (`goldenWaterV3`). Water is often the largest mesh (SEA spans the whole map), so every water vertex carries 3 dead bytes of CPU writes + GPU upload.
+- No focused static regression test guards the merged typed-attribute path; `test/pushface-color-neutral.test.js` covers color *bytes*, not the GPU upload path.
+
+## Current state
+Branch `opencode/voxel-vertex-color-uint8` from fresh `origin/master` `2ef15cca`. PC health before: free RAM 4.94/15.86 GB (~31%), CPU 68%, free disk 188.95 GB — acceptable for one bounded local job. No competing implementation: `origin/ai/opencode/voxel-color-uint8` is a zero-commit stale fork at old master.
+
+## Target state
+Water meshes carry no `color` attribute; solid/translucent keep normalized Uint8 colors; new `test/voxel-typed-geometry.test.js` fails if water color data returns, if float color attributes return, or if the color/normal/uv attributes lose typed quantization.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `apps/voxel-world/client.js` (`pushFace` guards `arr.col`; `rebuildChunk`/`rebuildChunkIncremental` water buffer drops `col`; `makeGeometry` sets `color` only when `data.col` exists).
+- `test/voxel-typed-geometry.test.js` (new focused regression guard).
+- `WORK_IN_PROGRESS.md` (this entry).
+
+## Known risks
+- Must keep `test/pushface-color-neutral.test.js` green (color byte equivalence + no `clone()` per vertex).
+- Water shader must not break: it never reads `color` (`#include <color_fragment>` body is a no-op without `USE_COLOR`).
+- No other buffer consumer of `data.col` exists besides `makeGeometry`.
+
+## Tests to run
+`node scripts/check-js.js`, focused `node --test test/voxel-typed-geometry.test.js`, `node --test test/pushface-color-neutral.test.js`, `npm run check:fast`, full `npm run golden:check`, full `npm run check`.
+
+## Deployment / PR plan
+Commit once, push `opencode/voxel-vertex-color-uint8`, open one PR to `master` with evidence. No merge, no deploy.
+
+## Final evidence
+Pending local verification.
